      "narrative": "Mara Venn's lips press into a thin line. She glances toward the bar \u2014 toward Toran Vex \u2014 then back at you.\n\n**\"Toran Vex. Lockwright of the Kestrel Guild.\"** She keeps her voice low. **\"He's been the one oiling the Ash Gate's mechanisms and turning its keys for... must be five years now. Sworn to the Guild, bound by their oaths. He knows every tooth of that lock better than anyone alive.\"**\n\nShe watches Toran take a shaky sip of his drink.\n\n**\"Which is why it's so damn interesting that he's sitting here, drinking cheap ale, instead of standing at his post while the council debates what to do about the gate.\"**\n\nMara tilts her head, studying you. **\"You want my read? He knows something he's not saying. Whether it's about the lock, or about Bram, or about what came through that gate the night Bram died... that's the part he's not telling.\"**\n\nShe lets the silence hang, then adds: **\"He might talk to you. He might not. But if you squeeze him, squeeze gently \u2014 he's the skittish type.\"**..."
