      "narrative": "Mara Venn's eyes flicker \u2014 a crack in her composure. She opens her mouth, then stops. Her fingers drum once on the table.\n\n**\"Old Bram.\"** She says it flatly, but something in her voice doesn't land right. She's repeating what everyone knows, not telling you what you asked. **\"Bram sold passage. Collected the toll, turned the lock, worked the boat. Everyone in town knows that.\"**\n\nShe holds your gaze a beat longer than comfortable, then looks down at her cup. Picks at a chip in the clay rim.\n\n**\"That's who. Was.\"**\n\nThe silence stretches. She doesn't elaborate. Doesn't offer the name of a Guild handler, a partner, a successor, a second set of hands. Just Bram. Dead Bram. The convenient answer.\n\nA log shifts in the hearth. Toran Vex's glass clinks against the bar as he sets it down too hard.\n\nMara Venn hasn't looked back up at you."
    },
